# XML schema and layout conventions

Follow these conventions when creating or editing XML in this repository:

## Source content structure

- Compendium content files use:
  - `<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>`
  - `<compendium version="5" auto_indent="NO"> ... </compendium>`
- Source manifest files use:
  - `<source>` root
  - metadata fields (`name`, `abbreviation`, `publisher`, `category`, `description`)
  - nested `<collection><doc href="..."/></collection>`

## Collection structure

- Collection files use `<collection>` root.
- When including partial collections, use XInclude:
  - `xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"`
  - `xpointer="xpointer(/collection/doc)"` for collection roots
  - `xpointer="xpointer(/source/collection/doc)"` for source manifests
- Use repo-relative paths exactly as existing files do.

## Compatibility and naming

- Keep folder and file names import-safe (avoid spaces/quotes in new technical paths).
- Keep naming style consistent with nearby files (`source-*.xml`, `collection-*.xml`, `*-<abbrev>.xml`).
- For subclass or spell-list extensions, rely on existing merge semantics (matching `<name>` entries) rather than duplicating full base definitions.

## Validation expectation

- New or changed XML must be valid against the appropriate schema before completion.
